# x1_per_layer: retired 02_per_layer, ported with a gate. Off the published line (different program;
# baseline_script_md5 in RUN_META). Levers: s4_onnx_and_spill's five plus embed_chunk_cpu.
#
# reason     retired endpoint 629 MiB at 5.2x rests on this driver (convert, encrypt, run, discard one
#            sub-model at a time). Published floor = whole-model conversion (three 433 MB releases on
#            17.08. did not move the peak).
#              published line  s5_embed_chunk   2,056,996 kB   factor 1.738x
#              retired         02_per_layer       629 MiB      factor 5.2x, no gate
# seeds      retired ct.init() unseeded (os.urandom(8)); this port pins seeds as the published script.
# gate       exact gate fails (layer i+1's PRZS draws interleave with layer i's Beaver draws).
#            GATE-TOLERANCE.md: changed mask stream moves the observable 2.34 on 0.135 at 12 layers;
#            argmax flips for one seed in five at 1 layer. Phase B:
#            (a) summed transcript over fourteen sub-graphs = baseline 11,228,688,384 bytes;
#            (b) impl/equiv_per_layer.py (whole vs per-layer plaintext, exact).
# mask       extended mask built as all zeros (declared in the script); valid only for the all-ones
#            attention mask of this workload.
# expected   0.6 to 1.0 GB vs 2.06 (-50% or better); transcript unchanged.
SHAFT_SCRIPT=$BASE/bert_perlayer_cpu.py
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
SHAFT_INNER_ENV="SHAFT_EMBED_CHUNKS=16"
